<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Repoint Odyssey's two class-based unique-weapon rolls off the stock ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon
       onto our ThingSetMaker_UMWUnique. Two reasons:

         1. Hardening. ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon calls MakeThing(def) with no stuff. Our melee uniques
            are stuffable, so it logs a red "madeFromStuff but stuff=null" error and forces them to steel.
            Our class rolls a random stuff for stuffable candidates, so the error is gone.
         2. Pool separation. Our class keeps the comp-based candidate set MINUS our weapons, so the
            quest / orbital stash roll Odyssey's (and other mods') uniques but never ours — ours are
            reserved for our own pool (UMW_Reward_UniqueWeapon). Other mods' uniques are unaffected.

       Behaviour is otherwise identical by construction: ThingSetMaker_UMWUnique is a faithful port of
       the stock retry loop (make a random candidate, keep it if its REAL market value fits the window),
       so both consumers keep vanilla's "exactly one unique, any that fits" outcome. This matters for
       MapGen_OrbitalItemStash, whose call site passes a fixed (2200,2200) window and no countRange — a
       value-budget maker (ThingSetMaker_MarketValue, the class's previous base) inverted those semantics
       and skipped the unique in most stashes; the full worked comparison is in the class header. No
       fixedParams are injected: quality comes from CompUniqueWeapon.PostPostMake (Super) on the made
       thing itself, exactly as the stock class relied on.

       Each consumer is wrapped in a PatchOperationConditional keyed on the exact node we expect
       (thingSetMaker[@Class="ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon"]). If a future Odyssey restructure removes or
       renames it — or another mod repoints the same node first — the patch simply no-ops instead of
       erroring (in the collision case our weapons would leak back into that pool; accepted, since we
       cannot know the replacement class's semantics). The Class predicate also scopes the op to the
       unique-weapon option only (MapGen_OrbitalItemStash also has a stockpile sub-tree option). -->

  <!-- Reward_UniqueWeapon — used by the AncientMercenaries quest (QuestNode_Root_AncientMercenaries). -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingSetMakerDef[defName="Reward_UniqueWeapon"]/root/options/li/thingSetMaker[@Class="ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAttributeSet">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingSetMakerDef[defName="Reward_UniqueWeapon"]/root/options/li/thingSetMaker[@Class="ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon"]</xpath>
      <attribute>Class</attribute>
      <value>UniqueMeleeWeapons.ThingSetMaker_UMWUnique</value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- MapGen_OrbitalItemStash — the unique-weapon option of an orbital platform's item-stash room. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingSetMakerDef[defName="MapGen_OrbitalItemStash"]/root/options/li/thingSetMaker[@Class="ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAttributeSet">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingSetMakerDef[defName="MapGen_OrbitalItemStash"]/root/options/li/thingSetMaker[@Class="ThingSetMaker_UniqueWeapon"]</xpath>
      <attribute>Class</attribute>
      <value>UniqueMeleeWeapons.ThingSetMaker_UMWUnique</value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
